--- body ---
## Context

`erg --help --all` concatenates helpText entries that each open with `# erg COMMAND`
(H1 headings). In a combined manual document this is wrong: H1 is reserved for the
document title; command sections should be H2. Additionally sections run together
with no blank line separator, and a few literal strings (`--- log ---`,
`--- body ---`, format patterns) appear without backtick formatting.

## Actions

1. In `help.go`: change every `# erg COMMAND` opening line to `## erg COMMAND`
   (12 entries). This keeps standalone `erg COMMAND --help` output correct as H2
   sections within a document; the assembly step adds the H1 title.

2. In `main.go` (`--help --all` loop): prepend a `# erg manual\n\n` title and
   insert a `\n` separator between sections. Do NOT add the blank line inside
   `helpText` strings — that would add a spurious leading blank when a single
   command's help is printed standalone.

3. In `help.go`: add backtick formatting to bare literal strings:
   - `validate` entry: `--- log ---`, `--- body ---` in the numbered list
   - `close` entry: bare `--- log ---` and log-line format string
   - `log` entry: bare `--- body ---` and `YYYY-MM-DDThh:mmZ LINE` format

4. Update `tests/test_docs.sh` and `tests/test_help.sh`: change
   `grep -c "^# "` → `grep -c "^## "` (two occurrences in test_docs.sh at
   lines 15 and 22; one in test_help.sh at line 114).

5. Regenerate `docs/erg-manual.md` via `make docs`.

6. Run `make test` to confirm all suites pass.

## Test

```sh
build/erg --help --all | head -1    # must be "# erg manual"
build/erg --help --all | grep -c "^## erg "   # must equal 12
build/erg --help --all | grep -c "^## erg "   # sequential sections separated by blank line
build/erg validate --help | head -1  # must be "## erg validate FILE..."
```

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `build/erg --help --all` first line is `# erg manual`
- [ ] `build/erg --help --all | grep -c "^## erg "` equals 12
- [ ] Each section in `--help --all` is preceded by a blank line
- [ ] `build/erg validate --help | head -1` starts with `## `
- [ ] `--- log ---` and `--- body ---` literals in affected entries use backticks
- [ ] `make test` passes
